findings.cause:
mod/UE4SS/AC8SurvivalMode/Scripts/sv_coop.lua hostPlane (0.73.79 :466, HEAD :505): `if SPC.alcnPool and a and SPC.alcnPool.set[a] then return end` runs before u.n/id/'bd'. clientPlane (0.73.79 :1041, HEAD :1154) skips the same way.

The set holds the parked pools' raw addresses (sv_alicorn.lua:112-114). It is only replaced when the next Alicorn spawns (:60), never cleared when the unit is removed and its 131 pool planes are destroyed (30 s deferred). UE reuses the freed blocks for new AI planes, so a later plane at a pool address is taken for a parked pool:
- the host sends no 'bd' id and tracks it in no M.byId, so it never sends a 'dn';
- the joiners' copies never bind, become strays after STRAY_S 15 s, are torn down unpaid, and the joiner sends 'jn' (at most once per 120 s);
- the rs|j repair re-sends only the ids the host has, so the cycle repeats.

Address reuse itself is inferred: addresses aren't logged. The 0-vs-18 split at the removal time, the first stray 3 minutes after it, and the high-ord skew all fit it.

findings.evidence:
Late parts (r20-31 average, ms a tick; early values in brackets):
- allies 14.8 (0.6), of which allies/counts 12-14;
- coop 14.0 (2.4);
- rounds 9.6 (1.2);
- leave check 4.0 (0.4);
- hud 3.6 (0.4).
At about 7 ms a call, the allies, coop, hud and leave parts alone are roughly 27 of the 35 ms of SV_UnitAlive a tick. Of the callers below, only the rounds' and the Spaceport's go through ALIVE at HEAD.

The ALIVE budget floor is RATE_MIN 8 asks/s (sv_spawn.lua:155-160, ALIVE.tick refreshes every watched unit about once a second). At 7 ms a call that is >= 56 ms/s, about 14 ms a tick. That is about what the rounds' once-a-second loops cost in 0.73.79, so it should flatten the 'rounds' bursts rather than lower the average (inference; Saint Alessia's 0.73.81 run is the one to check).

